The paper’s definition is stricter than “proper coloring plus length-two checks” in one subtle way: there are two distinct color types. A distance-1 color class must be independent, while a distance-2 color class must have pairwise graph distance at least 3. The paper also explicitly marks several small parameter pairs as polynomial-time, so I’m screening those out and examining its actual NP-hard reductions—especially Theorems 5, 6, 8, 14, and 15—rather than relying on the proposed random planar planting.
