codex
The 200,000-sample gate is behaving as expected but is expensive because every sample currently rebuilds the same suppressed core. I’ll preserve the exact verifier semantics while removing that repeated preprocessing from the measurement path if this run confirms it is the bottleneck.
codex
The cube-chain construction passes the quick structural checks I can run independently (20 distinct canonical keys; all declared cheap attacks fail; reference decoder verifies at about 146,400 counted operations). One important audit caveat remains: cubic bipartite cores admit polynomial 3-edge-coloring by repeated matching, and two-edge-cut structure has linear-time decomposition algorithms. I will not let a deliberately slow cut scan stand in for the strongest known method; the final Track B account must distinguish the natural coloring algorithm from the compact peeling route, or this family’s hardness claim would be overstated.
