codex
A stricter G4 audit found a decisive flaw in the affine prototype: the statement identifies a noncollinear anchor triangle, so a reader gets for free that its three values are a permutation of 0,1,2. That collapses the true candidate language from roughly \(q^3\) to six interpolated rules; sampling uniform coefficients was not structure-aware. I’m treating that prototype as failed rather than preserving its misleading 0/200,000 score.
