307:\begin{proposition}\label{prop:2_k_npc_tool}
308:    For every integers  $k \geq 1$ and $g \geq 3$, there exists a $\colo{2}{k}$-colorable graph $G$ of girth at least $g$ with a vertex $s$ such that in any $\colo{2}{k}$-coloring of $G$, $s$ must be colored with a distance-2 color if and only if there exists a graph $G'$ of girth at least $g$ that is not $\colo{2}{k}$-colorable.
