638:    Let $S$ be the set of vertices of $G$ of degree at least $N$, $N$ to be determined later. We start by constructing the sets $S'$ and $S_1, \dots, S_k$ from $S$ as in Lemma \ref{lemma:connected_dominant_kind_of}. Since for every $i$, $j$, $\dist_G(S_i, S_j) \ge 4$, then for every $i$, $j$, $\dist_G(N_G[S_i], N_G[S_j]) \ge 2$ so $G[N_G(S')]$ is an outerplanar graph and therefore is $3$-colorable. Since we can $2$-distance $f_3(N - 1)$-color $G - S$ and $\colo{3}{|S'|}$-color $G[N_G[S']]$ such that the vertices in $N_G(S')$ are only colored with distance-1 colors, the by Remark \ref{rem:colo_strat}, $G$ is $\colo{3}{f_3(N - 1) + |S'|}$-colorable. By Lemma \ref{lemma:connected_dominant_kind_of}, $|S'| \le 3|S|$ and since $G$ is planar, $|S| \le 6n/N$. Therefore, we can upper-bound $f_3(N - 1) + |S'|$ by $3(1 + o(1))N/2 + 18n/N$, and by taking $N = 6\sqrt{n}/\sqrt{3(1 + o(1))}$, we manage to use at most $6\sqrt{3}(1 + o(1))\sqrt{n}$ distance-2 colors as desired.
