The mathematical verifier and construction are internally consistent in the current audit, but the ladder has another design weakness: it grows the 8-vertex witness rows along with the graph and eventually stops on the effort cap. I won’t claim that as an unqualified scaling strategy. First I’m running the official bare hardening harness as required; its result will determine the actual shipping rung (or whether this family must be parked/rejected). The run owns and overwrites the bare transcript, as specified.
