codex
The first official hardening attempt could not make a single scored call: the configured OpenRouter key is over its total limit (HTTP 403), and the harness correctly aborted instead of counting that as model failure. I’m continuing with reversible local work, but I will not manufacture a “hardened” verdict.

I also found a way to improve the witness itself before final verification: each 8-vertex cube patch is uniquely pinned by its two boundary ports. Returning those two vertices per peel is still an executable certificate—the checker tries only the nine possible incident-edge pairs and reconstructs the eight vertices—but cuts the hard answer from 80 IDs to 20 without asking the checker to solve the instance. This keeps the mathematics and removes most transcription burden.
