codex
The port-pair certificate verifies across 175 construction cases through the maximum supported size. The first 200k-sample density run exposed a performance issue in the test itself—not the verifier: it was redoing bounded graph traversals for every obviously wrong first pair. I’m replacing that with an exactly equivalent precomputed set of valid first port pairs, while still sending every survivor through the public verifier.
